      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Given that $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(24{x}^{4}+20)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $y$ as a composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061u,\\,u=24{x}^{4}+20.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\sec^{2}\u2061u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=96{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\sec^{2}\u2061u\\cdot 96{x}^{3} \\\\  & =96{x}^{3}\\sec^{2}\u2061u \\\\  & =96{x}^{3}\\sec^{2}\u2061(24{x}^{4}+20).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
